  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_melt_wide_to_long(records: list, id_vars: list, value_vars: list, var_name: str = 'variable', value_name: str = 'value') -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Melt Wide to Long** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_melt_wide_to_long(records: list, id_vars: list, value_vars: list, var_name: str = 'variable', value_name: str = 'value') -> list:\n    return pd.melt(pd.DataFrame(records), id_vars=id_vars, value_vars=value_vars, var_name=var_name, value_name=value_name).to_dict(orient='records')\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
